From 72cb7e81346a2f44bc50598748e67017b77ebfcd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 08:46:58 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 26/58] phy: apple: t6050: park the PIPE from a dummy producer
 on any clock

At the first controller reset the USB3 PIPE mux is expected unset (0),
on the dummy producer (2) or already parked (0x42). When nothing has
reset the controller domain since boot, as on a boot without the
SPTM, the mux reads 0x22: the dummy producer on another clock. The
park then refused it and dwc3 failed to probe.

The park clears the clock field before it selects the dummy producer
and its clock, so start from any clock while the producer is the
dummy one.

Developed with Claude Code.
Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
---
 drivers/phy/apple/usb-t6050/apple_t6050_usb3_pipe.h | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/apple/usb-t6050/apple_t6050_usb3_pipe.h b/drivers/phy/apple/usb-t6050/apple_t6050_usb3_pipe.h
index f70f6f109038..8414ff1cebb6 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/apple/usb-t6050/apple_t6050_usb3_pipe.h
+++ b/drivers/phy/apple/usb-t6050/apple_t6050_usb3_pipe.h
@@ -23,7 +23,9 @@ apple_t6050_usb3_pipe_cold_dummy(const struct apple_t6050_usb_io *io)
     if (io->read(io->context, 44, 0x1c) & 1)
         return -1;
     mux = io->read(io->context, 44, 0x0c) & 0x73;
-    if (mux != 0 && mux != 2 && mux != 0x42)
+    /* Unset, or already on the dummy producer (1:0 = 2) with any clock: when nothing
+     * has reset the controller domain since boot, the mux can read 0x22. */
+    if (mux != 0 && (mux & 3) != 2)
         return -1;
     if (mux == 0x42)
         return 0;
